  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "ui-how-to-pick",
      "x": 820,
      "y": 60,
      "w": 320,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "All three are the SAME window with the same data \u2014 squint at each and ask which one you'd screenshot for the release page.\nA mix is fine too: e.g. Velocity's chrome with Studio's icon warmth. Say what you like and I'll build it into the real CSS."
    },
    {
      "id": "radical-premise",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 400,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "Round 2 breaks the formula, not just the paint:\n4 \u00b7 Island \u2014 Liquid-Glass world, queue as a Dynamic-Island pill.\n5 \u00b7 Flight Control \u2014 the pipeline IS the app; browsing demoted to rails.\n6 \u00b7 Commander \u2014 AI-native, no panes: one command field + activity cards (classic panes one keystroke away).\nAny of these can keep Studio (2) as the calm base theme underneath."
    },
    {
      "id": "color-premise",
      "x": 2100,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 340,
      "page": "page-3",
      "text": "DECIDED: Clay is the default theme, Cobalt the selectable light alternative, Iris the dark scheme \u2014 all user-selectable like today's four themes.\nSame mini-UI, six palettes \u2014 the hex chips at the bottom of each board are the actual tokens I'll install."
    },
    {
      "id": "product-plan",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -170,
      "w": 420,
      "page": "page-4",
      "text": "The agreed shape: Studio dual-pane is the default Browse mode \u2014 efficient find-and-queue, with Island's big omnibar up top. Once transfers are running, the Browse/Flight toggle lights up and flips to the Flight Control pipeline view (here re-skinned into Studio's light language).\nDouble-click on a remote file already queues it into the other pane's folder \u2014 shipped behavior.\nStill open: the accent color \u2014 pick one on the Color page."
    },
    {
      "id": "round5-premise",
      "x": 2720,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 380,
      "page": "page-5",
      "text": "Four more radical structures, all in the Studio/Clay-ready light language:\n7 \u00b7 Deck \u2014 bento home: the night's work at a glance, browse one toggle away.\n8 \u00b7 Timeline \u2014 transfers as a chronological story with inline actions.\n9 \u00b7 Starmap \u2014 sites as islands on a map; drag files onto a node, routes fly.\n10 \u00b7 Ambient Widget \u2014 minimized warpseed becomes an always-on-top pill.\nThese can be extra modes beside Browse/Flight, or stay ideas."
    }
  ],
